@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Evaluation algorithm for one chunking strategy
start
:Load SQuAD v1.1 (train + dev):
490 Wikipedia articles, 10,570 dev questions;
:Join paragraphs of each article into one document,
keep gold answer offsets (start, end);
:Split every document into chunks
(Fixed-N with step N - overlap, or Paragraph);
:Build BM25 index over "title. chunk text"
(k1 = 0.9, b = 0.4);
repeat :Take next dev question q;
  :Mark chunks of the same article that fully
  contain a gold answer span as relevant;
  if (Any relevant chunk?) then (no)
    :Count q as "answer split";
  else (yes)
  endif
  :Retrieve top-40 chunks by BM25 score;
  :rank(q) = position of first relevant chunk (0 if none);
repeat while (More questions?) is (yes)
->no;
:Compute Hit@k, MRR@10, budget-Hit,
bootstrap 95% CI;
:Paired McNemar tests on Hit@5,
Holm correction;
:Write summary.json and per_question.csv;
stop
@enduml
